# Line-ending policy.
#
# Shell scripts MUST keep LF. With core.autocrlf=true a re-checkout rewrites
# them with CRLF, which breaks a `#!/bin/sh` shebang on macOS/Linux
# ("bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M") and makes `exec` of a script unreliable under
# MSYS2 / Git-Bash on Windows. The publish-hygiene hooks in scripts/git-hooks
# have no file extension, so they are pinned separately.
#
# This matters here because the hook scripts are executed on every commit.
*.sh                text eol=lf
scripts/git-hooks/* text eol=lf
